 N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"74d4ec40a76d09bc5cbaa3688df909a24ceb0d2c65cd426869f2dbce8c100173","compact":"f91f405e60d06c57950724052578e2213cf3c29d1de52c70d1bffff59b98a3df","nasal":"f736fae9dd4b9d2a68f6a2e57d3b00061c9db94abbea736e843f5a8b105dc08b"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-27-7","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":27,"verse":7,"english":"The earth, afflicted with perspiration and filled with new water, is emitting forth vapour like to Sitā racked with sorrow.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.864,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-28-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4027007","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"027d78bd17cdcd850161e3f07b03348801e71a01b52f8c10f7fc4ac292aa893e","compact":"fbc90497bc23801666b2f81a794653f5b30eef00cd7246bca60d17daab1e1ccb","nasal":"840a13ff54b4c5dbd540a69624745f49370ffd264be1413639292efd0a25fd35"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-27-8","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":27,"verse":8,"english":"Ketaka smelling breezes may be drunk up in the cavity formed by putting the hands together, like to cold water discharged off the clouds and mixed with camphor.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.629,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-28-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4027008","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c2c493ee8b87ca1814e716cd6b56d4b94f5df0aa7544d07924db460a37549781","compact":"8705d568161d18cc27b5c400a23b7c3d89f4556018a3e858534b966fcce6c1b2","nasal":"5b702c94555d59a4d38c65c36ebcea2df22c385157d3fb997e41352edb5d5e12"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-27-9","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":27,"verse":9,"english":"This hill, having blown Arjunas and Ketakas and rid of its enemies like to Sugriva, has been bathed with showers.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.867,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-28-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4027009","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"20ac2bca9825f96ec97c1f0cef451da4860b710a2edc06c555f494bb3d4d07e6","compact":"9763439d0c9a6c96384e7c6c5ab8cc4cdde67900fdfb99d3fd61ad25e3cd3239","nasal":"fe2cebf00b8f2a21924f2a5c5ba88c4a2561a855aee1d0d1d1a710a5da9a8651"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-27-10","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":27,"verse":10,"english":"These hillocks, having clouds for dark deerskins, heavy showers for sacred threads and having caves filled with air, are appearing like so many Brahmins who have finished their studies.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-28-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4027010","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bb1837beec108687218402c768b8affa8e94452bc7d28c3e6790b428b363a643","compact":"061cec4978c5daf342840cf3f8ff541a23c7f9f6fffc82ed61b4a7e4e18eb58a","nasal":"061cec4978c5daf342840cf3f8ff541a23c7f9f6fffc82ed61b4a7e4e18eb58a"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-27-11","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":27,"verse":11,"english":"The sky, being struck by thunders like to so many golden lashes, is, as if, groaning under a deep mental agony.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.73,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-28-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4027011","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9bd2a5d3c931a8d904710d567c0d82f03dd9b6dfc3c0b62d2d51d05de579b831","compact":"2a4c74bad6e94c75ae88c0a035e12360fcbb65f5683dea0e16b58ea7ce1b3ba6","nasal":"68a4f64d436dc19999fd2496d7ab23d21e1d580ee9317a76c1cfe9289ef61c25"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-27-12","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":27,"verse":12,"english":"Methinks, the lighting, shining by the violet clouds, is appearing like to the poor Vaidehi at the lap of Rävaņa.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-28-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4027012","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"02bf0720d5e594ab6cd7abd83b4cfb3c6b52cd0f44a30e5dd6cdb4a2be07e6f7","compact":"73eec2020609c7e707fd886661feb7458fd35b222567a100256881ab9a9b9617","nasal":"47e165c1c8b4d35108feec5821466e5edfb4a11cbeb41ada04c19fd85d68bbfe"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-27-13","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":27,"verse":13,"english":"These quarters, enveloped with clouds and having therefore the Moon and stars hidden, are indeed very pleasant to those who are under the influence of Cupid","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-28-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4027013","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4918cdcb56849a55be97052c418e859ea726ba728e0a285f985dccac70c4b56c","compact":"756008181eec5b8c3cdaeb39b5f14a9f9befa23c4710a327abca95bae0fe4a7f","nasal":"756008181eec5b8c3cdaeb39b5f14a9f9befa23c4710a327abca95bae0fe4a7f"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-27-14","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":27,"verse":14,"english":"Behold, O Saumitri, on the summits of the hill the flowery Kuțajas enveloped with the vapour arising out of the earth, gladdened at the approach of the rainy season and exciting my amour who am stricken with grief.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.853,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-28-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4027014","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"37f4513ea4ead6eb16152093abb3140de4c43b35f64da488ccc37df19da80b35","compact":"59eaf70c58abb191b65cfd63d6387b85c1bf9d91fbe7e3c6a7d3fadc1a82bc83","nasal":"59eaf70c58abb191b65cfd63d6387b85c1bf9d91fbe7e3c6a7d3fadc1a82bc83"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-27-15","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":27,"verse":15,"english":"(In this season) the dust is watered, the air is saturated with dews, all the evils of the summer are stopped, the kings no longer proceed on royal marches and those journeying in a foreign land return their native homes.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.735,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-28-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4027015","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5f2984b0f978a9f02ce30cec625b0f93fd0b47c88cf8c0d0e52031c0b0805737","compact":"6aa778775f4e872dc618524b2fac48d111a04a688df5643280eb26cfeed1c543","nasal":"06fe7e3c0f777f20bc50d457ca42ff06c3708cf057b085e065c86c360cce3066"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-27-16","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":27,"verse":16,"english":"The Cakravākas along with their mates are proceeding, being desirous to live in the Mänasa Sarovara, and in consequence of incessant rains, chariots and other conveyances cannot pass along the wayfares.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.742,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-28-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4027016","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2558026cfb39b34a47383ebd48093e038c12196e92bf6448c72b78e453f542e2","compact":"85cace72756b660bbc355a30bfd0c78bbfd6786c6a2f32ab78339c2281d8ba3d","nasal":"8dc7cffb4f9cfe58486249a4f487ec2e64dd8b8c636069282e4bf8454a56d55e"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-27-17","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":27,"verse":17,"english":"Somewhere hidden, somewhere open, the sky, covered with clouds, appears like a vast ocean, being encircled here and there with hills.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.833,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-28-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4027017","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d6faaf36bb132081ac9d29aa7609dba46fabc7a9ef86002b8d6d3a96316dbeec","compact":"2473aa7a9d31b6123b1c3570ed5979e1cb15220cf2907667f3d4b7ed162a2c4f","nasal":"d93c129d279bbb0166d5d5fdbda6f2cef299423ca4d29d50b36755278d48478c"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-27-18","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":27,"verse":18,"english":"There speedily pass by the hill streams, being resounded with the cries of peacocks, carrying with the current Sarja and Kadamba flowers and having their coppery contents mixed with the metals of the mountain.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.663,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-28-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4027018","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"40eac438b6133dbe88f811e141a6295b1f72a500648245a6dc3cf79319b261b0","compact":"cd9450e4b63e09f4197ac73bd6f9ed04e67da51373e5826b3fad2044591ad0af","nasal":"29226e2ec2d31b40c3ae81254bf9afbbf452dc0e8eafd1bc8909f9d54d161572"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-27-19","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":27,"verse":19,"english":"People (in this season) live upon Inany a sweet rose-apple; and ripe mangoes, of diverse colours, being shaken by the wind, fall on the earth.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.889,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-28-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4027019","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b58452eeabe500f712e075c650938e700f7d872856a0bb55ca19e1d7603e76f5","compact":"a5ceb5b482bc180a4f6b591be434200c64f58b0d12ddcfa4cb4e0ea814f10c07","nasal":"279c73711b10d2271a6e2f5769c63ff3de1ff7f5a6986aed43d5d95ba77f0fa1"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-27-20","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":27,"verse":20,"english":"The clouds, resembling the summits of a mountain, having lightnings for pennons and cranes for garlands, are muttering like to infuriated elephants in a field of battle.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.913,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-28-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4027020","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"898512b201093db25399de5ac18e93ad8ea9f11a3ff3cd7d82297b090d5d3236","compact":"39b1ce227ecb193ff4400d2cf66559dc8e663faba15e982b4c0fbde6f2efc71f","nasal":"6a7a6619ec9dc45ed403a57da7062227581e669ec7f1f1d42cf9fbffcb5ba925"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-27-21","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":27,"verse":21,"english":"And rows of cranes, fond of clouds, rising up in the sky, delighted and moved by the wind, are appearing like a garland of white lotuses, spread along the welkin.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.5,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-28-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4027021","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ab270fa41b33677ffdd23b4b71b5f85aafbad077aa5b9b0f81e1a5b620d4da50","compact":"84eeba8a89951815417e3dc50a30d76b2e0b453eb6d5cf865c8a5c4519a7ce62","nasal":"14433526714995d8a7902eb051b7813bdf13b1281c8f1f988423d4066dfe48e8"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-27-22","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":27,"verse":22,"english":"(In this part of the year) sleep is gradually overcoming the great God Nārāyaṇa, the river is flowing speedily towards the ocean, the delighted cranes are approaching the clouds and the damsels are proceeding towards their lovers.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.8,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-28-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4027022","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"42b0a25337fb45c7398f6b906b669fa19b34873ba4d3b6a49a9e6ef8d4c94ca8","compact":"2278f733693ed068dfde073bdceb1221663c4873e9f1094b95e10a15f2688b96","nasal":"66725cf7cb9c0c9116f60c113d6507efc96a522186d01db67b71875b3bcdbd24"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-27-23","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":27,"verse":23,"english":"The peacocks are dancing at the forest skirts, the Kadamba trees are covered with flowers, the bulls have become attached to her and the earth has become charming with corns and forests.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-28-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4027023","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a96336e82b5baaf501ab593929b6bdf5b2a25c7cc7725a77f76fe09f3e6c85ff","compact":"baf9ddad2487881818a41c1392c72b884ffde227b8f664f66a23cc89c06d849c","nasal":"d73d35017faa64722209507c3a106a598189575963fe143b21b6249b313e9089"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-27-24","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":27,"verse":24,"english":"The rivers are flowing by; the clouds are discharging waters; the infuriated elephants are emitting terrible roars; the forest-lands are growing more charming; persons, separated from their wives, are growing more anxious; the peacocks are dancing with delight and the monkeys are greatly comforted for Sugrīva's attaining to the kingdom.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.857,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-28-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4027024","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"be9759a9ddc9930ccef13506221f3d516f0d644933264bb654658d7923e1743c","compact":"cdd0e8d8b7837b5d6ad67fa456173e76112f022ef5e8ce1d3b473ad53d7880bc","nasal":"82505f6c1932e843e6e04c25deb84f9ba6aaf3c07a7b017311a8dbbbd332181d"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-27-25","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":27,"verse":25,"english":"By the fountains in he forests, the infuriated elephants delighted with the fragrance of the Ketaka flowers and maddened with the noise of the water falls, are emitting terrible roars along with the peacocks.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.522,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-28-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4027025","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8300297821cd78acf9df32ccc29022cde0b82b39361f13a1d8ef19d1b11778bc","compact":"a2892cd97af0b18f5b19819f36cf3443c877fd8da0e0f592af2ffb69236a6d9f","nasal":"3922d18886d0ed772e75698cd3f78a2d8b0ae8be0de907401bab6022d6f3900f"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-27-26","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":27,"verse":26,"english":"The black bees, resorting to the branches of the Kadamba trees and overwhelmed with showers, are, as if, slowly discharging their temporal juice-namely the honey of flowers collected by them ere while.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.849,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-28-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4027026","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c67e099e60b2ae0bc4f2763451a8459c2722ebe3ccb64ed72b13f8a8b9246c72","compact":"f955f0595164845c938bb651158f9aa8dee12e0667c3c47a12d2443443363e48","nasal":"4b7f732f5c18380b70f8b6a83a8fd0167284e0622dbef59512f1dab96afc41c1"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-27-27","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":27,"verse":27,"english":"The branches of rose-apple trees containing enough of fruits like to a collection of char coal are so appearing as if the black bees are drinking the juice thereof.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.817,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-28-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4027027","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7adeb20392a56cff13f4a067ef5375f7a2b1bd20cef2e05ad5ee1734c75f5b6e","compact":"9d416768e6e3490c27e6163438668a9b4f029dc306c25b0567edb255