od":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-28-35"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4027030","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"08e158c48a9dd76b9cdb23d7b82ae16668327e259db04886a59fcd3dce9e3447","compact":"0843e4fdf845846fdb3018ac0feb73345cf298b7e3e938333a67fa50099ea938","nasal":"1307015e5b001dbe06550c6973a52d4b54b76fb18f49ca265988384dc56fcfbe"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-27-31","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":27,"verse":31,"english":"Clouds, big with new waters coming in, contact with violet ones are appearing as such; and sometimes, touching the hills brunt by forest-fire, are appearing like deep-rooted hills.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.912,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-28-40"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4027031","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"eb6682f84743f4b52e7b30f0de0a26eb927afc3d3b794838df20b8797674d088","compact":"3922328fd1189cf63383daa1e4d2655fb3a563876f0d89d39841fbc6f98e20e0","nasal":"27170b241f7683b70c6d409e9d543db24af92d192b44c67d795602d25685813d"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-27-32","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":27,"verse":32,"english":"(In this season) the elephants are infuriated, the bulls are delighted, the lions have grown more powerful, the hills are charming-the kings are devoid of all active pursuits, are the Lord of celestials is engaged in sport with clouds.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.725,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-28-43"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4027032","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c5b45739fa164bbf7f60d68c44112fc4c49ae2a4f34de9060f601a0d990f8f93","compact":"ae7fece7f9b24aa61c88afebe722371605f62ce5e250e88ef06f2c9af27373dc","nasal":"ca0630b32b00acc11de139a641aed62e30e1a0194ff538fd5893a863fb2cce90"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-27-33","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":27,"verse":33,"english":"The royal marches are all stopped, and the soldiers, who have already marched are waiting in the way-hostility and wayfares have been equally blockaded by water.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.803,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-28-53"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4027033","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0e184fdfb7e86accc763b7a058a1e1b9cd4c429ccba16e3722fffdb2c53b0f60","compact":"69a88145bab67615ba1153bb2885335c9ae89c9bcd4f315a0c026f2061387076","nasal":"ea5dab1e20ba97394ef7e2a2bf8e599d16d23f1391321cba8c80596efb07578e"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-27-34","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":27,"verse":34,"english":"This month of Bhādra is the time of studying for those Brahmins, who chant Sāma Vedas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-28-54"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4027034","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3730768d8bff178ee36c3325418795580c2fb41d951107550c33874064ddcda6","compact":"0f15723cf5ddf9300a5c54cbb0436894310f87d2c9a2640595f0b94ff11203ca","nasal":"0f15723cf5ddf9300a5c54cbb0436894310f87d2c9a2640595f0b94ff11203ca"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-27-35","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":27,"verse":35,"english":"Having roofed all his houses and stored up his food, Bharata, the king of Kosala has set upon the performance of Așara sacrifices.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.66,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-28-55"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4027035","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"aebd49e89d78a990d81db687f5c3e8f5a545ba7ff62c2dd14e074f33b06d17b2","compact":"b3f7d166c0835516fe3fe69f49d2bd4607826417a3193d45751bb7fcfe3aba14","nasal":"b3f7d166c0835516fe3fe69f49d2bd4607826417a3193d45751bb7fcfe3aba14"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-27-36","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":27,"verse":36,"english":"The river Saraju is now brimful with water. Seeing me return as if Ayodhyā herself is making a delightful noise.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.879,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-28-56"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4027036","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0a01052b039fda5f289453d2c3453b0a0395fdc710706cd1483af0048258d104","compact":"99697e1fcf711bb0eb439ef1b69009c7d8d35f4097e7379707b8626759d55757","nasal":"75995714181cc4fabc172c17639fa3aaef505c4dab5ca44a010ac80e5ef82b56"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-27-37","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":27,"verse":37,"english":"Clearly manifest are now all the signs of the rainy season and Sugrīva, rid of his enemies, established on the vast kingdom, and regaining his wives, has attained to best felicity.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-28-57"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4027037","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a07ea0e5c5b91d7a09597f4987071926b93bfe48d4eda29744da4be942369902","compact":"07eed6085e99e75fda03187af0f66b2ce5c6d7a4b3d5ed62510eb0c8972682f5","nasal":"07eed6085e99e75fda03187af0f66b2ce5c6d7a4b3d5ed62510eb0c8972682f5"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-27-38","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":27,"verse":38,"english":"And I am, O Laksmana, waning every day like to the banks of a river, being separated from my spouse and deprived of my vast kingdom.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-28-58"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4027038","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"24b23b0c3b3a94cf6544e3528ece230e90da5b6c2123d224196b8cf4d72e9bc4","compact":"8484b6f7e08134cdfa63d842e0afb93e833d8894af3b513eacfc1e81463791ea","nasal":"c3108ae8b15e47015819da7310f653107fd2b0f71539a837ea5bcbcb90243cf2"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-27-39","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":27,"verse":39,"english":"Immense is my grief, inaccessible is this rainy season and mighty is my enemy, Ravana; methinks it is impossible for me to bring about the discomfiture of my foe.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.746,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-28-59"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4027039","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a45f047cf75a9192f886410ca54b42be4e0f284f392df62ca7d50969a676c8b5","compact":"3dc2a55b9b24686874ba9113fbb24d9e8297fa766c8a1dd93a77e816ff82b11e","nasal":"3dc2a55b9b24686874ba9113fbb24d9e8297fa766c8a1dd93a77e816ff82b11e"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-27-40","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":27,"verse":40,"english":"Owing to the unfitness of the season (for marching against my foe) and the wayfares being inaccessible, I cannot possibly request Sugrīva (to march) although he is prepared to abide by my mandate.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.886,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-28-60"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4027040","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e7e2d3c807255a2574d7d18c281d5544cb890c4234b19ace5c709139c2fb4c41","compact":"71928aa4f236c6671e05b84c0d07515be2d1fcbae15f3626077f3cc5141e833b","nasal":"71928aa4f236c6671e05b84c0d07515be2d1fcbae15f3626077f3cc5141e833b"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-27-41","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":27,"verse":41,"english":"Moreover after a good deal of affliction he has regained his wives, and my service is of very great difficulty; so I do not wish to request that monkey-chief now.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.914,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-28-61"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4027041","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"67c2a65a1ac9f5a727f7f719a76a025b55d38b429655c99f9ea03c0f8baa6510","compact":"d6dcb3a2b56106d8d703ea1954c15766fbe9236da6eda81c5dadd0d13ae7f8fd","nasal":"d6dcb3a2b56106d8d703ea1954c15766fbe9236da6eda81c5dadd0d13ae7f8fd"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-27-42","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":27,"verse":42,"english":"Forsooth, shall Sugrīva think of the benefits (he has received from me) after enjoying rest for sometime, when the time for action shall arrive.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-28-62"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4027042","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7b8a146215a05eb3a0b8fb6b5311df8a8506001ad0c266650db42d7b0b37cfd1","compact":"0ca56d7ba25a86ed4437196e3841dfc7e52863a6002f68ddfd58dd490a60dbef","nasal":"0ca56d7ba25a86ed4437196e3841dfc7e52863a6002f68ddfd58dd490a60dbef"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-27-43","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":27,"verse":43,"english":"Therefore I shall, O Laksmana, live here, awaiting the pleasure of Sugrīva and the clear currents of the rivers (the autumn).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.875,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-28-63"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4027043","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"79f68b9d4da68b5e6eabe250c12b03b740a305c929bce3266cd86eb9ba67a4c8","compact":"061cd9d3228d2050ee47c29105f3beaf398f8d20573a4144b05425c796d125e7","nasal":"061cd9d3228d2050ee47c29105f3beaf398f8d20573a4144b05425c796d125e7"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-27-44","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":27,"verse":44,"en